==Battleground==
*10 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*2 [[Hyppoh]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*1 [[Maawth]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns as the boss.
**6 [[The Thrillerz]] spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Maawth]] spawns.
**2 [[Zomboe]]s spawn, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
**1 [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] spawns.

==Strategy==
An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies stage. By now, it is expected you have all the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]], meaning you should have both the [[Aqua Crystal]] [[Treasure]] and the [[Plasma Crystal]] [[Treasure]] in every [[Into the Future]] chapter. The Zombie enemies are the main threats, The Thrillerz have a pretty powerful [[Single Attack]] even at 100%, Lord Gravey has well-rounded stats, and Zomboe's burrow can sometimes mess things up despite being pretty weak, they also all come out of nowhere, as none of the other [[Continuation Stage]]s from [[First Round (Expert)]] had any Zombie enemies except for a Zoge. The Alien enemies aren't too big of a deal aside from Bun Bun Symbiote, and maybe even Maawth if you haven't brought a lot of good units to outrange Maawth.

As always, stall the beginning enemies for as long as you can before hitting the base. When you hit the base, start sending out any [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] cats you may have brought, and send out any [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] units you may have brought as well, like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]. It would be wise to target Bun Bun Symbiote first, as he has less health and bad [[Wave Attack]] RNG can ruin a run. Once Bun Bun Symbiote is gone, the stage should be fairly trivial, as Lord Gravey cannot push that far on his own.

